From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.networking.connectivity: profiles, names, host names, cost, adapter, usage, events (3564)

windows.networking.connectivity: profile lists, names, cost, adapter, usage, host names and status events

NetworkInformation.GetConnectionProfiles returns one profile per connected network of the network list
manager; profiles are keyed by their network (GetInternetConnectionProfile picks the network that reaches
the Internet, else the machine's connectivity as before). A profile now answers ProfileName and
GetNetworkNames (IVectorView<HSTRING>), GetNetworkConnectivityLevel per network, GetConnectionCost (the
network list manager's cost for the connection that reaches the profile's gateway), GetDataPlanStatus (no
plan data), NetworkAdapter (speeds and IANA type from the adapter table, NetworkItem, adapter id,
GetConnectedProfileAsync through an operation that is complete when created), GetLocalUsage and
GetLocalUsagePerRoamingStates (the interface's byte counters since boot) and NetworkSecuritySettings.
GetHostNames lists the computer name and the addresses of every connected interface through the
HostName factory, GetLanIdentifiers is empty (no link-layer discovery data on the host).
NetworkStatusChanged keeps its handlers and tells them from iphlpapi's interface and address change
notifications (register on the first handler, cancel on the last). One generic read-only vector
(IVectorView/IIterable/IIterator) serves HSTRING, ConnectionProfile, LanIdentifier and HostName; the
IIterable/IIterator ids are declared in the IDL.
